Z||000000||Bruce||12-28-2000||08:28 PM||||Just had the distributor replaced; new plugs and plug wires, but the car slips in 2nd and 3rd. Any ideas?||||reg||1
Z||000001||Old Lar||12-28-2000||08:41 PM||||What do you mean by slipping in 2nd and 3rd?<P>Transmission slips?  Car engine skips?||||reg||1
Z||000002||Bruce||12-29-2000||11:14 AM||||Idle is smooth; feels like the trans. slips.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Old Lar||12-29-2000||11:54 AM||||I'm assuming you have an automatic transmission.  Check for proper fluid level, fluid color (red hue), no burnt oder.  If these check out, transmission service may be in order.  High milage transmission rebuid may be in order.<P>When I've had slipping transmissions, it was due to low fluid.  When the internal clutches were going, the car would not shift gears, time for overhaul.||||reg||3
Z||000004||Bruce||12-30-2000||12:18 AM||||It's a 4 speed manual.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Old Lar||12-30-2000||07:40 AM||||The Haynes manual: Under slips out of gear.<P>1. Worn or improperly adjusted linkage.<BR>2. Tranaxel loose on engine.<BR>3. Shift linkage does not work freely, binds<BR>4. Iput gear bearing retainer broken or loose.<BR>5. Dirt between clutch cover and engine housing.<BR>6. Worn shift fork.<P>Could be the start of linkage problems.||||reg||1
Z||000006||theogre||12-30-2000||01:33 PM||||I don't think he ment comes out of gear... only way a manual tranny can "slip" is if the clutch is messed up. ||||reg||1
Z||000007||Phaeton||12-31-2000||02:09 PM||||Itsy bitsy teeny weeny low pressure factory clutch.<BR>Get ahold of George at the Fieroshop for some alternatives. <A HREF="http://www.fieroshop.net/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroshop.net/</A> <BR>||||reg||12
